# Thingino SNMP Monitor — camera configuration
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/thingino/monitor.conf and edit it.
#
# Format: IP|COMMUNITY
#   IP         — IPv4 address of the camera (this is its identity)
#   COMMUNITY  — SNMP community string (set in camera's Web UI → Services → SNMP)
#
# The camera's hostname and description are queried live over SNMP, so
# nothing else is stored here. If a camera is replaced by another unit
# on the same IP, the monitor picks up the new identity automatically.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments.

# 192.168.1.100|mysecret
# 192.168.1.101|mysecret
# 192.168.1.102|anothersecret
